OL,3,AFailed asylum seekers face removal
OL,4,Awithout five-day notice period
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe government is to change the law so
OL,7,Fthat it no longer has to give failed
OL,8,Fasylum seekers notice before they are
OL,9,Fremoved from the country.
OL,11,FCurrently, people are given five
OL,12,Fworking days' notice but ministers
OL,13,Fbelieve this leads to last-minute
OL,14,Fappeals which delay the process.
OL,16,FUnder the new rules, once an asylum
OL,17,Fclaim fails, the Home Office would have
OL,18,Fsix months in which to remove the
OL,19,Fapplicant without telling them in
OL,20,Fadvance.
OL,23,APub: 17-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
